implementationPlan.description:
THE ROUND TRIP (DoD 4) - `apps/daemon/src/deployment/deploy-target-ledger.test.ts`, against a REAL store.

Dispatch `deployment.set_target` through the registered handler and assert:
(a) the target is READ BACK from a real store with EVERY member asserted - network, sshTarget (including the `null` case for a local daemon), url;
(b) the read comes through `decodeDeployTarget` / the `DeployTargetPort`, not by reaching into the event payload - that is the path the deploy engine actually uses, and a test that bypasses it proves the store wrote something rather than that the engine can read it;
(c) SETTING TWICE REPLACES: bind, bind again with different values, assert the read-back count is ONE and the values are the second binding's;
(d) an unbound environment answers `DEPLOY_ENVIRONMENT_UNBOUND` with its code AND layer;
(e) an invalid payload refuses `DEPLOY_TARGET_INVALID` with code AND layer and writes NOTHING - assert the store is unchanged by reading it back, not by trusting the return value.

Teardown in a `finally`: every store handle and temp directory released on the throwing path too (epic rail 4).

MUTATE AND CONFIRM RED for (c): make the write append instead of replacing, confirm the count arm reds, restore and prove it. That file is new and untracked until staged - back it up out of tree and prove the restore by SHA256 in a separate call if you drill before staging.
